# Helios 3D shadow analyst panel (helios3d.panel). NOT INSTALLED: every line
# below is commented out on purpose. It is a separate unit from
# helios-local.service, so a live restart never drops it, and it is not in
# Celery beat. Nothing schedules it; pair it with a timer only by decision.
#
# Before installing:
#   1. Dry-run by hand (reads only, calls no model, writes nothing):
#        venv/bin/python -m helios3d.panel run --limit 5
#   2. Check that the live-lane gate can read the live broker (read only):
#        venv/bin/python -m helios3d.panel gate
#   3. Choose the compute budget and set it in the
#      EnvironmentFile: HELIOS3D_PANEL_BUDGET=full or shortlist (plus the
#      shortlist rule), HELIOS3D_PANEL_MODEL (and any per-role
#      HELIOS3D_PANEL_MODEL_<ROLE>), HELIOS3D_OLLAMA_URL. Every setting is
#      listed in helios3d/panel/config.py.
#   4. Stop it at any time without systemctl: touch logs/.h3d_off (the kill
#      file is checked before every model call). Remove the file to resume.
#
# Model co-residency: if HELIOS3D_OLLAMA_URL is the live server, a panel
# model other than the one loaded there makes Ollama swap models and starves
# the live 72B (2026-10-25), and a different num_ctx makes Ollama reload the
# same model. Set HELIOS3D_LIVE_OLLAMA_URL (required) and, when sharing,
# HELIOS3D_LIVE_MODEL: the runner then refuses to call unless every role's
# model is the live model and HELIOS3D_PANEL_NUM_CTX=32768 (live's num_ctx,
# agents/analyst.py). Any other model belongs on a separate Ollama instance.
#
# [Unit]
# Description=Helios 3D shadow analyst panel (h3d.panel_output, h3d.pm_verdict)
# After=network-online.target redis.service
# Wants=network-online.target
#
# [Service]
# Type=oneshot
# WorkingDirectory=/home/YOUR_USER/Desktop/trading_bot
# EnvironmentFile=/home/YOUR_USER/.config/helios3d/panel.env
# ExecStart=/home/YOUR_USER/Desktop/trading_bot/venv/bin/python -m helios3d.panel run --apply --limit 20
# Nice=10
# TimeoutStartSec=6h
#
# [Install]
# WantedBy=multi-user.target
